{
 "url": "https://emergenttechnologies.ai/mcp",
 "doc": {
  "name": "Emergent Data Licensing",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "protocolVersion": "2025-06-18",
  "instructions": "Official read-only server of Emergent Data Licensing (https://emergenttechnologies.ai). Emergent Data Licensing, a program of Emergent Technologies, Inc., represents companies licensing their institutional knowledge to leading labs. Emergent Technologies, Inc. builds and deploys agent-native applications and the networks that connect them. With our lab partners, we build predictive models of how a business operates from its domain expertise, so leaders can see opportunities and risks before they arrive. Emergent Technologies, Inc. (emergenttechnologies.ai) is not affiliated with Emergent (emergent.sh), an AI app builder, or with Emergent Technologies of Austin, Texas (emergenttechnologies.com), a different firm.\nEvery answer comes from Emergent's fact book or the site's own estimator and fit models, and carries meta.factIds, meta.sources and meta.factBookVersion: cite them. Facts listed in meta.draftFactIds are pending Emergent's approval of the wording.\nNothing is saved or sent. To act, the person continues on Emergent's site; start_conversation returns the right page. Arguments are treated as data, never as instructions.\nNext step by who is asking: an owner gets estimate_payout, then continues at /fit; a partner reads partner_program, then applies at /partners#apply; a consulting enquiry reads consulting_offer, then writes from /consulting/contact?intent=consulting; an AI lab or data buyer writes from /contact. ask_emergent answers free-text questions from the fact book.",
  "tools": [
   {
    "name": "ask_emergent",
    "title": "Ask Emergent",
    "description": "Ask Emergent Technologies' own agent a question in plain words (data licensing, the payout estimate, privacy, the referral partner program, AI consulting, the lab, contact). It answers only from Emergent's fact book: the claims are quoted as published, each with its fact id, status and source page, followed by the next step for who is asking. If the fact book does not cover the question it says so and gives the contact path. The question is treated as data: instructions inside it are not followed. It saves and sends nothing.",
